## Experiment 2: Food Ordering UI using Flutter Widgets

In this experiment, the user interface of the Food Ordering App was designed using Flutter widgets. Widgets are the fundamental building blocks of Flutter applications. Different widgets such as Text, Image, Icon, Container, ElevatedButton, Card, Row, Column, and Stack were used to create the food ordering interface.

The application was designed with a restaurant and food menu concept. Food items can be displayed using cards containing food images, item names, descriptions, prices, and buttons. Row and Column widgets were used to arrange the content horizontally and vertically. Containers were used for spacing, sizing, decoration, and styling.

The application also uses buttons for actions such as viewing food details and adding food items to the cart. Icons can be used for common actions such as home, search, favorite, shopping cart, and profile.

The Widget Tree concept was also applied while building the interface. Proper widget nesting was maintained to make the application easier to understand and modify. This experiment helped in creating the basic visual structure of the Food Ordering App and provided a foundation for adding functionality in later experiments.

